um  good morning or good afternoon dear  attendees  um of the discovery user symposium 2020  and this is dr kombak from  precision pathology by a banking center  of  memorial sloan-kettering cancer center  in new york  um our ppbc is the core facility for  research operations in mskcc  consisting of histology and immunostore  chemistry  labs and the biobank  i myself i'm a pathologist i  did my medical training and residency in  turkey  in istanbul and i've been working  in this facility  for almost  15 months now under a supervision of  dr roll dr silber and dr bennett  and with a great team of course  in this presentation i will try to  demonstrate  our multiplex immunothe chemistry  experience with you  [Music]  immediate chemistry experience using the  discovery ultra platform  first of all i would like to quickly  revisit the basics first  immunostar chemistry is a widespread  technique  which we use in our daily practices for  tumor diagnosis  and classification prognosis  and prediction and also for selecting  candidates for targeted therapies  with ihc we can selectively identify  antigens with specifically binding  antibodies  and visualize antigen antibody  interaction  with detection systems  there are a lot of detection systems  which  are direct conjugate labeled antibody  method  indirect or sandwich procedure unlabeled  antibody methods  whitens tryptophan systems and alkaline  phosphatase labels and polyvalent  detection systems  the most common one ones we use are the  peroxidase antiperoxidase method  and the ap anti-ap method  from all of these  we also need chromogens to visualize the  end product  chromogen is a color producing substrate  which is  activated with the enzymatic reaction of  the detection system  chromogens are either peroxidase based  or alkaline phosphatase or glucose  oxidase based  the most common ones are dab  aec and fast strat we usually use  in our daily routine  new chromogens are also emerging such as  horseradish peroxidase-based ones which  i will talk in detail  later here's a  simple demonstration of most common  chromogens  on the left hand side you'll see the red  membrane  staining of aec and on the right side  you will see  the brown membrane staining of the ap  there's been a growing demand  about immunostar chemistry like if  only they could label more than one  marker per section  or assess combined markers like pd1 and  pdl1  or be able to see the distribution of  immune cells  and interaction between between cells  and or  molecules and in the meanwhile to  preserve tissue and time  which these ideas led us to the concept  of  multiplex immunostory chemistry  today we have a bunch of different  techniques for  multiplex immunothe chemistry procedures  which are bright field based metal based  chip cytometry or dna barcoding based  methods  today i'll be talking about the  discovery ultra staining system which is  an example of bright field-based  multiple immunostatic chemistry  it is an automated platform for research  purposes  and it works with sequential cycles  without these staining steps in between  it uses chromogens with broad absorbance  spectra  and doesn't need as integrated scanner  or imaging microscopy or analytics  software  it is easy to perform and easy to  evaluate  and you only need a conventional bright  field microscope to evaluate the end  product  on discovery ultra staining system you  can combine  ap and hrp-based chromagens  in sequential cycles  so um to explain that after  de-paraffinization and pre-treatment  there  are consecutive cycles and antibody  denaturation steps in between  each sequence consists of primary  antibody  secondary antibody enzyme conjugate and  chromogen incubation periods  and after the last cycle there is  a step for counterstaining with a  hematoxylin  however five plex design consists of  pdl1  pd1 cd68 cd8 and cd3  antibodies and we combined  ap based red and yellow stains with  hrp based dab purple  and teal  pdl1 is the programmed  death elegant one which is a  transmembrane protein  that has been speculated to play a major  role  in suppressing the adaptive part of  immune system  that means the upregulation of pdl1 may  allow cancers to evade the host immune  system  many pdl-1 inhibitors are in development  as immuno-oncology  treatments and are showing good results  in clinical trials  so pdl-1 assessment has been a center of  interest for a while  just to show simple examples for  antibody chromogen couples in our design  you see here the bronze membrane  staining for  of the dab for pdl one  purple for pd1 there are some  teal staining and cd8 positive cells  around but the purple staining is still  distinguishable  red for cd68 to highlight macrophages  tl4 cd3 and yellow for cd8  um these two are usually intermingled  in our samples  we we applied this five plex protocol on  our collection of pontium or  tissue microarrays and these pontium  rtmas are  separate three separate blocks um with a  total of 144 cases  which are carcinomas of of different  origins like  lung colon stomach and gallbladder and  pancreas  as well as gastrointestinal stromal  tumors  sex course normal tumors and soft tissue  and bone tumors melanomas and  other rare and miscellaneous tumors  this application allowed us to have a  broad opinion on the distribution of  pdl1  and pd1 expression and the immune  response  in different type of tumors  here is an example  of a pdl-1 positive core  it is a nice display of the tumor and  the strong pdl bone positivity  and the  polyphonic immune response around it  and also within the tumor  if we look closer we can get a better  detail  of the pdl1 expression in the tumor  and also the immunoprofile of the  infiltrating cells in the scene  in some of the course we observed some  focal mild red staining mainly on tumor  cells  which seemed like a precipitation issue  and improved um  with an additional step of reaction  buffer rinse  and  after that addition i can say  that the background staining is minimal  as you can see here  even in areas with dense immune  infiltrators  a lot of positive cells  um another material we run the  procedure is the pancreatic ductal  adenocarcinoma  tissue microarrays which are  two separate tma blocks carrying  a total of 87 cases  45 of which are female patients and the  rest of  42 is are male patients  also 36 of them are short-term survivors  and the rest are long-term survivors and  the median age is  70.  i displayed this image to  give some opinion about how i  interpreted this  tma sections with the five flags  on the left hand side you will see the  green annotations for tumor areas  and on the right side you will see the  pink annotations for peritumeral stroma  as is known the tumor and stroma can be  very intermingled and pedex  and they both contribute to the  malignant process but still  this discrimination provided me so much  information about  the tumor-associated immune response  here is an example of a pita case with  some degree of pdl1 expression  [Music]  and also we can see the  infiltrating immune cells with  a different immunoprofile  you can also measure the proximity of  pd1 positive cells to the nearest tumor  cell  with using a simple  image analysis program or it can be a  freeware program online  i would also like to talk about another  design we  created using the new chromogens which  are  the beta products of roche tissue  diagnostics  and they're not commercially available  yet and they're still in development  and they are tirement based hrp mediated  chromogens  the procedure is sequential just  like the fiveplex design  this time only with the hrp-based  chromogens  so similarly after the paraffinization  and pre-treatment  there are three consecutive cycles  consisting of  primary antibodies secondary antibody  enzyme conjugate and chromogen  incubation  and in the end there is a step for  counterstain with hematoxylin  in this design we combined pdl1  and ttf1 pdl1 matching with  red chromogen and ttf1 matching with the  yellow chromogen both  are hiv-based and we  used six pulmonary adenocarcinoma cases  with  varying levels of pdl1  expression  here is the yellow nuclear staining for  ttf1 in tumor cells  and the red membrane is staining for  pdl1  and the combination you see here  um you see here the pdl one positive  and ttf1 highlighted tumor cells in the  upper half  there are also some other red staining  cells  beneath that part but  most of them are macrophages um  actually it is hard to discriminate on  monostain  whether the pdl one positive cell is  a really a tumor cell or a macrophage  especially in tumors with solid pattern  like this  and abundant macrophages around  they can be positive for pdl-1 and  easily be  misinterpreted as a tumor cell  so marking tumor cells with ttf1  at the same time um facilitates the  interpretation  and therefore provides  a better pdl one scoring  similar um to the  to this image in this one there is an  area of macrophages in the center of the  image  which can easily be identified as  pdl-1 positive tumor cells on monostain  and this is  another case showing a smaller  percentage of pdl1 positivity  and as you can see the staining  intensity is  variable from weak to strong in the  sample  um as an adjunct we decided to add  cytokeratin as a third antibody in the  design  so it would cross check and enhance the  efficacy of ttf1  um to detect the tumor cells  creating a discernible transition from  nuclear yellow staining to the membrane  and spread  staining  we use the same six lung cancer  cases again for this design and  you see here a part of benign epithelium  um staining with um  blue for cytokeratine and  yellow for ttf1  this is the case with a lower pd l1  positivity i showed you earlier with the  double design  now the tumor cells are highlighted both  with  a yellow staining of ttf1 and  blue cytoplasmic staining of cytokeratin  blue cytoplasmic staining off the  cytokines and makes it  easier to detect the red membrane  staining staining of pdl one  now let's review some comparison images  with the ab  this is a case with um  this is the case uh negative for um  pdl1 there is some  mild normal background staining with dab  which we don't see in the triplex design  and in this sample  it's a case with mild to moderate  positivity for pdl one  and i try to capture  the exact same areas to compare the  staining quality  i can say that  [Music]  the variation in staining intensity is  with the red chromogen is very similar  to dab  and the percentage of positivity is also  accurate  another case with moderate staining  red staining is moderate in intensity  likewise  the same subpopulation however on the  left side  seems um somewhat paler in both stains  this is partially because of the  infiltrating  lymphocytes which can easily be  recognized and ignored with ttf1 and  cytokeratin negativity in the triplex  design  and an example of strong positivity  when the membrane staining is strong we  usually get some cytoplasmic reflection  of  it with any chromogen  blue cytoplasmic staining of  cytokeratine also helps with that  by overruling that infusion-like  staining from the membrane  now a closer look and for the eggs to  the same area  the red membrane is staining is very  sharp and strong  just like the ab which gives me the idea  that it can be  implemented to her2 staining  also and also  a lot of other combinations can be  created  with other antibodies  so based on our experience i can say  that  discovery ultra staining system is  an efficient automated platform for  research purposes  on this platform you can combine ap  and hrp based chromatins and it's very  easy to perform  with the stainer you don't need to  integrate a scanner  or an imaging microscopy or analytic  software  and it's easy to review you only need a  conventional bright field microscope and  you see  all the  chromogens on the same slide under light  microscope  there may be a minimal overlapping  and minimal background staining and due  to  the utility of multiple chromatins but  if you have such a problem i can suggest  to add a reaction buffering step  after the problematic chromogen  incubation which  provided improvement in our case  and also the successful integration of  hrb based neurochromogens into the  sequential multiplex ihc  procedure is also promising for the  future of this technique  i would like to thank you for your  interest and  attendance on behalf of my team  and if you ever want to get in touch you  can just  easily send an email to me or to dr roll  and we will be very happy to communicate  with you  thank you

